======================================================================
Interactive usage
======================================================================

To start an interactive shell using the remote-ssh environment:

  bash --rcfile "@INSTALL_DIR@/shell/rc.sh"


======================================================================
SSH configuration
======================================================================

Add the following entry to your local SSH configuration
($HOME/.ssh/config):

  Host @HOSTNAME@
    HostName @IP_ADDRESS@
    User @WHO_AM_I@
    IdentityFile ~/.ssh/<ssh-key>
    RequestTTY yes
    RemoteCommand bash --rcfile '@INSTALL_DIR@/shell/rc.sh' -i


Then connect normally:

  ssh @HOSTNAME@

This will start an interactive session with the remote-ssh shell
initialised automatically.


======================================================================
Optional Git setup
======================================================================

To enable the bundled Git defaults from `dots/git/config.base`, run:

  remote-ssh-git-setup

This creates `dots/git/user.local` from the example if needed and adds the
base config via `git config --global include.path ...`.
